# The headless acceptance run, built NATIVE via hxcpp.
#
# Same source as acceptance.hxml — the real lab modules with the null gfx
# backend — on a compiled target instead of the neko VM. Useful when `hl` is
# unavailable (the local runtime segfaults on any bytecode) and as a second
# opinion on the shared-sim port: neko carries native 31-bit ints and relies on
# Haxe's Int32 semantics for the uint32 RNG, while cpp has real 32-bit ints, so
# agreement across both is stronger evidence than either alone.
#
# The WINDOWED client cannot come here: Heaps targets hl or js only (see
# build.hxml). This is the netcode, not the renderer.
#
#   haxe acceptance-cpp.hxml && ./bin/cpp/Acceptance
-main Acceptance
-cp src
-cp ../../../../colyseus-haxe/src
-lib colyseus-websocket
-lib tink_http
-cpp bin/cpp
